<title>NETHERLANDS: Stork unit wins Gulfstream order.</title>
<headline>Stork unit wins Gulfstream order.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch industrial systems group Stork NV said on Wednesday its unit Fokker Aerostructures had won an order from U.S. aircraft maker Gulfstream Aerospace Corp.</p>
<p>Fokker Aerostructures, part of maintenance and components company Fokker Aviation which was taken over by Stork in 1996, will re-design and deliver lightweight composite rudders.</p>
<p>&quot;The contract value totals some tens of millions of U.S. dollars,&quot; Stork said in a statement. First delivery is planned in the course of next year.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
